HST Office: centimetres are the default measurement unit in Writer, Sheets, Slides and Draw, whatever the locale.

Upstream picks the unit from the locale: Sheets, Slides and Draw read Layout/Other/MeasureUnit/Metric (cm) or
NonMetric (inch), and Writer (also Writer/Web) has no Layout/Other/MeasureUnit default, so it falls back to cm or
inch by the locale's measurement system. An en-US system therefore showed inches on the rulers and in Format › Page.
Both variants are now centimetres (2) and Writer's and Writer/Web's MeasureUnit default is centimetres. A unit the user
chose in Tools › Options stays in the user profile (registrymodifications.xcu) and still wins over these defaults.

